Use the explicit MOZ_DRM_DEVICE path for VA-API probing when glxtest cannot
report a standard DRM render node in a DRM-less Termux environment.

Termux does not expose a standard `/dev/dri` device list, while the Wayland
Mesa stack can still provide a usable KGSL render node through `MOZ_DRM_DEVICE`.
The graphics probe otherwise tries to enumerate DRM devices with libdrm and
records a warning when that enumeration fails. Firefox treats that warning as
a failed glxtest and disables all hardware video decoder gfx variables. Honor
the explicit Termux render-device override before probing libdrm, and use the
unversioned Termux libdrm name for the fallback path.

--- a/widget/gtk/GfxInfo.cpp
+++ b/widget/gtk/GfxInfo.cpp
@@ -422,4 +422,12 @@
     NS_WARNING("Failed to parse GL version!");
   }
-
+#ifdef __TERMUX__
+  if (drmRenderDevice.IsEmpty()) {
+    const char* drmDeviceOverride = PR_GetEnv("MOZ_DRM_DEVICE");
+    if (drmDeviceOverride && *drmDeviceOverride) {
+      drmRenderDevice.Assign(drmDeviceOverride);
+    }
+  }
+#endif
+
   mDrmRenderDevice = std::move(drmRenderDevice);
--- a/toolkit/xre/gfxtest/glxtest.cpp
+++ b/toolkit/xre/gfxtest/glxtest.cpp
@@ -159,7 +159,11 @@
 #  define LIBEGL_FILENAME "libEGL.so.1"
 #  define LIBDRM_FILENAME "libdrm.so.2"
 #endif
